    chore(board): file today's learnings — 4 rows, one already fixed
    
    Bane asked what the runs taught and whether it got prioritized. Filed:
    
      REPORT-1 (P1) the hourly report mislabels the actor — it credited JEV with
                    unaided decisions in long_0927_llm2, which is the pure-LLM arm
                    where JEV is never called. Root cause in aipp_hourly_facts.py:
                    no decision_mode read at all, and JEV-shaped field names
                    (jev_answered, top_jev_missing_classes), so it cannot tell
                    System One from System Two. Same report also invented an
                    "Oak's Lab not proven" blocker for a run seeded at Pallet Town,
                    because it renders the ladder as required-in-order.
      ARM-1   (P1) OWNER DECISION: the shipped default (jev) is the arm that
                    cannot leave Pallet Town — 0/5 vs pure LLM 6/6, and today the
                    pure-LLM arm reached Viridian in 50 minutes. Options recorded;
                    not acting without the owner's call.
      BOOT-1  (P1) long_run.py:47 hardcodes data/boot.state, which probes as
                    Oak's Lab — NOT the Pallet Town state every baseline in
                    data/baselines/ was measured on. A run launched the obvious way
                    is silently incomparable. Also: the driver passes no
                    decision-mode flag, so a run's arm is not in its own record.
      EFF-1   (P2) autonomy 1.00 while ep001-ep008 all ended inside Red's House 1F —
                    the metric cannot see a loop. Needs decisions-per-transition
                    and backtrack rate beside autonomy.
    
    Already fixed today: the win condition was a touch test that halted a 4h run at
    54 minutes (f4d51a4 — now a HOLD; guard green on all four checks).
    
