 {"id": "REVIEW-1", "title": "SECURITY: the dashboard ships a default API key in source, binds 0.0.0.0, and prints the key to stdout", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Third-party hands-on review, reproduced on a scratch instance I started myself (port 4701, since stopped). src/dashboard/main.py:37 is `API_KEY = os.getenv(\"PTP_API_KEY\", \"ptp-secret-key-12345\")` — a committed default. REPRODUCED: `curl .../status` -> HTTP 401 unauthenticated, but `curl -H 'X-API-Key: ptp-secret-key-12345' .../status` -> HTTP 200 (and /metrics -> 200). The docstring 8 lines above (:46-53) claims the opposite: '...which leaves authenticated calls at 401 rather than falling back to a committed default.' Code contradicts its own comment. Three compounding factors: (1) default bind is 0.0.0.0 (`host = os.getenv(\"PTP_DASHBOARD_HOST\", \"0.0.0.0\")`, :506-509); (2) startup prints the key to stdout (`print(f\"API Key: {API_KEY}\")`, :512) so it lands in logs and scrollback; (3) the key unlocks POST /control/start, /control/stop, /control/pause, /control/command — remote control of a running agent. THE REPO IS PUBLIC (github.com/wojons/ai_plays_poke), so the default credential is public. Done-when: API_KEY has no default (fail closed when PTP_API_KEY is unset), PTP_DASHBOARD_HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1, and the key is not printed. Estimated 45 min total.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:45:38.639400+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-27 20:10:00", "commit_hash": "692cddd", "worker_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "worker_provider": "xkiro"}
 {"id": "REVIEW-2", "title": "The requirements files have drifted from pyproject: pytest-benchmark and pytest-timeout are in NEITHER", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Third-party review, measured on a fresh clone. Of the 13 dev dependencies declared in pyproject.toml [project.optional-dependencies].dev, TWO appear in neither requirements.txt nor requirements-dev.txt: `pytest-benchmark>=4.0` and `pytest-timeout>=2.1`. CONSEQUENCE, reproduced: `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt && python -m pytest tests/ -q` -> 5 ERRORS in tests/test_performance.py::TestBenchmarks::* with `fixture 'benchmark' not found`. The two manifests are hand-maintained mirrors of pyproject and have drifted apart. Done-when: the requirements files are GENERATED from pyproject (or the drift is removed and a test asserts parity), and `pytest tests/test_performance.py` collects with 0 errors on a clean clone. Estimated 30 min.", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:45:38.639400+00:00"}
